Carry `seed` from an Anthropic Messages request into the converted request.

vLLM's Anthropic endpoint (vllm/entrypoints/anthropic) converts a Messages
request into a ChatCompletionRequest with an explicit field list, and `seed`
is not on it: the Anthropic wire has no seed of its own, and the request
model ignores unknown fields rather than refusing them. A caller on that wire
therefore cannot pin the sampler, silently — the request succeeds and the
output is simply not reproducible.

This deployment's whole reproducibility contract rests on a pinned seed (the
handler injects one when the caller omits it and echoes it in the
reproducibility block), so the Messages wire needs the same field the
chat-completions wire has. `seed` joins the request model beside the other
vLLM-specific fields that are not in the Anthropic spec (`cache_salt`,
`vllm_xargs`, …) and is passed through the converter.

Pure Python, no behaviour change for a request that omits it.

--- a/vllm/entrypoints/anthropic/protocol.py
+++ b/vllm/entrypoints/anthropic/protocol.py
@@ -138,6 +138,13 @@
     top_p: float | None = None

     # vLLM-specific fields that are not in Anthropic spec
+    seed: int | None = Field(
+        default=None,
+        description=(
+            "Random seed for the sampler, as on the OpenAI-compatible "
+            "endpoint. Required to make a response reproducible."
+        ),
+    )
     cache_salt: str | None = Field(
         default=None,
         min_length=1,
--- a/vllm/entrypoints/anthropic/serving.py
+++ b/vllm/entrypoints/anthropic/serving.py
@@ -485,6 +485,7 @@
             temperature=anthropic_request.temperature,
             top_p=anthropic_request.top_p,
             top_k=anthropic_request.top_k,
+            seed=anthropic_request.seed,
             cache_salt=anthropic_request.cache_salt,
             kv_transfer_params=anthropic_request.kv_transfer_params,
             ec_transfer_params=anthropic_request.ec_transfer_params,
